/E (Home Start Nottingham Coordinators have been building a partnership with Helen Murphy at Nottingham College who runs several family literacy and numeracy courses throughout Nottingham, both city and county. The courses are aimed at parents with preschool age children and focus on skills and knowledge such as getting ready for a transition to school or nursery, engaging in literacy and early phonics through play, and fostering family bonds and interaction through story telling and play. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (The first group, 'Reading Rucksacks', was attended by 3 Home Start families and a further 4 families who benefited from the support of Home Start coordinators in Forest Fields/ Carrington. The second group, All the Early Years, is under way in Clifton with 4 Home Start families attending and promotion to the wider community taking place. The activities vary each week, encouraging play and creativity, during the first group each family were encouraged to try out activities relating to the story that week, including receiving a copy of the book, meaning the child had activities and the books to engage with their family with at home.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13]
>>
